          "en": "have all possible permissions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 62.99,
          "end": 66.23,
          "en": "For example, something like reading or writing files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.23,
          "end": 68.53999999999999,
          "en": "or sending network requests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 68.53999999999999,
          "end": 71.13,
          "en": "or listening to network requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 71.13,
          "end": 73.06,
          "en": "These are all operations,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 73.06,
          "end": 77.52,
          "en": "that are always unlocked and possible with node,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 77.52,
          "end": 79.57,
          "en": "any node script can do anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 79.57,
          "end": 82.01,
          "en": "When you execute a JavaScript file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 82.01,
          "end": 85.63,
          "en": "with node, that file is able to do everything,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 85.63,
          "end": 88.4,
          "en": "it could delete all files on your system,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 88.4,
          "end": 91.42,
          "en": "and nothing would stop it from doing that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 91.42,
          "end": 94.07,
          "en": "Therefore, when you execute code with node,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 94.07,
          "end": 96.56,
          "en": "you have to trust that code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 96.56,
          "end": 98.97,
          "en": "either because you wrote it on your own,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 98.97,
          "end": 101.71000000000001,
          "en": "or because it's some third party library,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 101.71000000000001,
          "end": 103.06,
          "en": "which you trust,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 103.06,
          "end": 107.14,
          "en": "because code could potentially do a lot of bad things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 107.14,
          "end": 110.22,
          "en": "With Deno, there's a different model, that's being used.",
